From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: separate native pixel DMA and gate readiness

Bind the pixel stream as a platform component with a separate DMA domain.
Wait for both providers before publishing video nodes. Select one buffer
owner for VB2 queues, internal allocations and HFI context-bank flags.
Cover encoder input and decoder output. Reference the allocation owner
until each internal buffer is freed through that same device.

Use the native binding's MMIO pages and pixel child. Preserve the DMA
aperture and legacy platform paths. Let the platform bus own DMA setup
and default-domain lifetime. Do not import Android DMA callbacks, manual
domain ownership or fixed board IOVAs.

Protocol: Qualcomm GPL-2.0-only VIDC memory extension, HFI buffer packet
and Cliffs context-bank table in OnePlus SM7675 modules/DT revision
1138e00fee63582a0cc6a53af3286621786827b7. Compare Uke OEM kernel5712080a,
DT94c84aeb and upstreamf47d2236 separately.

Keep this candidate inactive. It adds no native core match, board DT,
firmware payload, secure context or physical codec claim. Resolve open
sessions and failed-PAS forced removal before native activation.

Signed-off-by: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>

